From: sie-mcp web <web@sie-mcp.local>
Subject: [PATCH] tci: size-specialized guest memory ops (exact-mop fast forms)

The generic qemu_ld/qemu_st interpreter cases pay, for every guest memory
access: the full mask computation of tci_tlb_probe() (s_mask, a_mask, atom
class from the stream mop), a size+sign switch over the access itself, and
(after 0011) a wasm call into tci_qemu_ld/tci_qemu_st that re-probed the
TLB with identical inputs (measured dead: 0 hits in >1M calls - removed).
Counters show the fast paths are THE hot path: ~5.9M loads + ~2.4M stores
per wall second at 15M guest insns/s on this host, and the op mix is
dominated by st32/ld32u/st8.

Measured on pmb887x/ARMv5 (S75 fullflash, every plain data access carries
MO_ALIGN|MO_ATOM_NONE|size|sign, LE): for that exact family the generic
probe reduces to
    (addr & (TARGET_PAGE_MASK | size-1)) == tlb_addr
so eight new appended opcodes (tci_qemu_ld8..st32) bake the mask in as a
compile-time constant, skip the size switch, and go straight to the
access.  The rrm stream word carries only the mmu_idx; the case
reconstructs the full MemOp on the (cold) fallback path so the exact mop
survives for the slow path.  Non-matching mops keep the generic ops.
Counters confirm 100% of guest memory traffic flows through the new ops
(231M loads + 96M stores in 60 s, zero emitter rejections of live mops).

Also: tci_qemu_ld/tci_qemu_st no longer re-probe the TLB (dead, see
above), and a small cold-path diagnostics counter set (include/qemu/
wasm-diag.h, wasm_memstat export, tools/memstat.mjs) counts slow-path
entries: helper fallbacks, MMIO dispatches, TLB fills.

Measured (S75, headless Chromium, v=2..7 window, 4 interleaved A/B pairs
against the 0011 build rebuilt byte-identical under the same conditions):

  window   base 40.6 / 34.4 / 34.9 / 34.5 s
           cand 34.1 / 33.9 / 34.0 / 34.0 s   (candidate wins every pair;
                 -1.4..-16%, larger under host load; candidate also much
                 tighter across runs)
  finalV@110s  base 90.9 / 99.7 / 97.8 / 102.3   cand 113.8 / 120.3 /
               121.1 / 120.1   (+18..25% boot progress; the phases after
               v=7 are memory-op dense and benefit most)
  insns@110s   ~1.67-1.70G both (window-external phases shift)

Boot verified: no >>EXIT<<, 90s ab soak clean, v progresses past 120,
serial/LCD healthy.  Native TCI builds get the same interpreter cases
(generic TCI, like 0003/0008/0011).
---
